  "Question": "What is the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) in the expansion of \\((1+x)^3\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The binomial coefficient corresponding to \\(k=2\\) is \\(C(3,2)=3\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Expand by multiplication\n\nSince the exponent is only \\(3\\), multiply the factors directly:\n\\[\n(1+x)^3=(1+2x+x^2)(1+x)=1+3x+3x^2+x^3.\n\\]\nThe \\(x^2\\) term is \\(3x^2\\), so its coefficient is \\(3\\).",
